WEBVTT

00:00.470 --> 00:03.730
<b>Unbeknownst to all...</b>

00:07.610 --> 00:09.790
The transaction supposed 
to happen just up ahead.

00:10.480 --> 00:13.510
We have to hurry,
 before the Port Mafia notice.

00:13.510 --> 00:15.410
Dammit, you old geezer, why?

00:16.150 --> 00:18.310
Just kill the freaking detectives.

00:18.890 --> 00:20.830
<i>They got here ahead of us.</i>

00:20.830 --> 00:22.790
Remember what the boss said?

00:22.790 --> 00:26.930
Francis might be with the military police, 
so don't go near their business.

00:26.930 --> 00:29.800
Yet they ignored the boss's orders 
and went off on their own.

00:29.800 --> 00:32.090
They're disrespecting the boss!

00:32.480 --> 00:35.810
Looks like you can't let go of your 
old gangster habits, Tachihara.

00:35.810 --> 00:39.470
The Port Mafia's actions are not determined 
by whether or not there is disrespect,

00:39.470 --> 00:42.400
but by whether they are 
faithful to the boss's wishes.

00:43.450 --> 00:46.340
Don't let anyone hurt the Agency.

00:46.340 --> 00:48.600
Protect them with your life.

00:48.600 --> 00:51.110
That is the order we were given.

00:51.110 --> 00:55.990
In other words, the boss knew they were 
about to engage in dangerous business.

00:55.990 --> 00:57.870
<i>Mori-sensei knew that?</i>

00:57.870 --> 01:01.480
There you have it, detectives.

01:02.590 --> 01:06.540
That Mori-sensei sure is 
a worrywart, isn't he?

01:06.950 --> 01:08.420
He doesn't need to worry.

01:08.420 --> 01:11.050
Your deal with Francis isn't a trap.

01:11.050 --> 01:11.890
Oh?

01:11.890 --> 01:12.790
How are you so sure?

01:12.790 --> 01:15.170
Atsushi believes him.

01:15.750 --> 01:21.060
Atsushi fought with him 
previously on the Moby Dick.

01:26.520 --> 01:30.200
Once you've bared your soul to someone 
by trading mortal blows with them,

01:30.200 --> 01:32.520
they won't be fooled by your lies.

01:33.240 --> 01:35.440
We're almost at the transaction site.

01:35.440 --> 01:36.450
Yeah.

01:36.450 --> 01:37.640
Here we go.

01:38.220 --> 01:40.880
We finally have hope of saving the Agency,

01:41.580 --> 01:43.370
but that's not all.

01:43.370 --> 01:47.960
The Agency shows its real strength when 
it's together, not when it's spread out.

01:47.960 --> 01:48.620
Yeah.

01:51.480 --> 01:53.520
I can't wait to meet the others.

01:57.160 --> 01:59.060
The car's here!

01:59.060 --> 02:02.100
We've been waiting for you! Atsushi-san!

02:06.810 --> 02:07.730
Kenji!

02:07.730 --> 02:08.520
Don't move!

02:11.610 --> 02:12.960
Targets surrounded!

02:12.960 --> 02:14.900
Now capturing the suspects!

02:15.190 --> 02:16.410
<i>Shit...</i>

02:16.410 --> 02:17.770
<i>I hope this isn't what I think...</i>

02:18.040 --> 02:19.070
Kenji-kun!

02:24.150 --> 02:25.030
<i>What the hell?</i>

02:25.350 --> 02:27.040
<i>An enemy ability?</i>

02:27.310 --> 02:29.550
<i>The ornamentation on that saber...</i>

02:29.550 --> 02:30.540
The Hunting Dogs!

02:30.540 --> 02:31.780
Everyone, run!

02:31.780 --> 02:33.280
The transaction was a trap!

02:33.280 --> 02:35.540
Francis has sided with the enemy!

02:35.790 --> 02:36.680
Damn it.

04:09.030 --> 04:12.580
Francis-sama, may I ask you something?

04:12.580 --> 04:13.560
What is it?

04:14.110 --> 04:18.030
Of the 78 strategy proposals I wrote,

04:18.030 --> 04:22.600
74 involved selling the Agency members' 
location to the government.

04:22.600 --> 04:28.950
It would be a good opportunity to make up 
for having crashed the Moby Dick.

04:29.250 --> 04:31.940
Why didn't you make a deal 
with the military police?

04:33.560 --> 04:35.210
Louisa-kun...

04:35.640 --> 04:39.570
Do you remember the time when
 we were reunited on the streets?

04:39.570 --> 04:41.360
I would never forget.

04:41.840 --> 04:43.160
Me, neither.

04:43.810 --> 04:47.800
Everything I ate tasted like sand.

04:47.800 --> 04:49.680
Even breathing was laborious.

04:50.160 --> 04:53.030
Despair takes away a person's 
ability to get back up on their feet.

04:53.490 --> 04:55.780
For the several months, until you came along,

04:55.780 --> 04:58.770
I hadn't even thought of 
rebuilding the organization.

04:59.440 --> 05:02.820
But the Agency got back up within an hour,

05:03.290 --> 05:06.140
and now they're fighting for their lives.

05:07.180 --> 05:10.270
I always side with the winners.

05:10.270 --> 05:13.740
And, in this fight, the Agency will win.

05:17.190 --> 05:20.950
Therefore, I will side with the Agency.

05:20.960 --> 05:23.960
<b>Episode 47</b>

05:20.960 --> 05:23.960
<b>In Lament of My 
Wingless Body</b>

05:28.050 --> 05:30.010
Dammit, they're all over the place.

05:30.370 --> 05:32.160
Squad A, Squad B, advance.

05:33.400 --> 05:35.450
Squad C, deploy thermal scopes.

05:35.450 --> 05:37.430
Don't let the one with the 
illusion ability escape!

05:37.980 --> 05:38.930
Kenji!

05:39.430 --> 05:41.840
I'm all right.

05:41.840 --> 05:42.810
This is nothing.

05:45.850 --> 05:47.270
<i>A raincoat?</i>

05:47.870 --> 05:49.820
<i>It's not even raining.</i>

05:50.740 --> 05:53.300
<i>Something feels off.</i>

06:03.350 --> 06:04.130
Kenji!

06:09.840 --> 06:11.370
I can't get the sword out!

06:11.780 --> 06:12.600
Move!

06:23.770 --> 06:25.020
Everyone!

06:25.920 --> 06:28.070
We're escaping into a secret
 Port Mafia escape route.

06:28.070 --> 06:29.100
Come.

06:30.290 --> 06:31.480
Understood.

06:36.040 --> 06:39.160
The squads on the ground have 
requested that we move out.

06:42.940 --> 06:44.040
Wanna?

06:55.430 --> 06:56.520
Let me see!

06:56.520 --> 06:57.690
I'll fix him.

06:58.630 --> 07:00.410
I told you.

07:00.410 --> 07:02.020
It was a trap.

07:02.410 --> 07:03.810
It appears so.

07:07.800 --> 07:10.250
<i>But something still seems off.</i>

07:11.070 --> 07:12.400
Yosano-san...

07:13.100 --> 07:14.990
Thank you very much.

07:14.990 --> 07:16.280
You've saved me.

07:19.320 --> 07:22.510
The Port Mafia's armed 
forces are returning fire,

07:22.510 --> 07:24.710
but their defenses are falling apart.

07:25.100 --> 07:29.740
If the five Hunting Dogs come, 
this escape route will be destroyed, as well.

07:29.740 --> 07:31.020
No.

07:31.020 --> 07:32.940
I suspect one of them is already here.

07:33.660 --> 07:34.940
That saber...

07:35.280 --> 07:37.160
It belonged to the Hunting Dogs.

07:37.550 --> 07:40.510
I'm told that the Hunting Dogs 
have superhuman physical prowess

07:40.510 --> 07:44.240
as well as exceptionally 
powerful special abilities.

07:44.690 --> 07:49.580
Each of them has the military power
 of a thousand special forces soldiers.

07:49.580 --> 07:50.860
A thousand?!

07:50.860 --> 07:52.790
They're freaks!

07:52.790 --> 07:54.870
And there are five of them?!

07:59.410 --> 08:01.520
Tanizaki, Kenji...

08:01.520 --> 08:02.750
We need to talk.

08:04.320 --> 08:05.540
Let's split up and run.

08:06.560 --> 08:07.610
We can't!

08:07.610 --> 08:08.750
We have to stick together!

08:09.100 --> 08:10.390
I know that.

08:10.790 --> 08:13.210
But right now, only one of
 the Hunting Dogs after us.

08:13.210 --> 08:15.470
If we split up, two of us will be saved.

08:17.180 --> 08:24.250
Mori-sensei mentioned a hideout for us 
and a designated vehicle for reaching it.

08:24.770 --> 08:26.140
Have they been prepared for us?

08:26.140 --> 08:27.920
They have.

08:27.920 --> 08:28.560
Good.

08:29.720 --> 08:31.390
Make me a promise:

08:31.900 --> 08:37.440
whoever survives will put their 
lives on the line to rebuild the Agency.

08:38.230 --> 08:39.320
Of course.

08:40.220 --> 08:41.540
Let's do it.

08:47.650 --> 08:50.010
You're about to enter a complex maze.

08:50.370 --> 08:54.220
Use this map to reach your escape vehicles.

09:08.780 --> 09:10.290
Please stop.

09:13.160 --> 09:14.310
What's wrong?

09:14.310 --> 09:15.670
I hear fighting.

09:15.670 --> 09:17.740
Lots of gunshots and combat boots.

09:18.880 --> 09:22.410
And familiar footsteps from underground.

09:23.620 --> 09:27.460
Wasn't there a secret Port Mafia
 passage in this area?

09:38.620 --> 09:39.660
Atsushi!

09:39.660 --> 09:40.370
Kyouka!

09:40.780 --> 09:42.050
Yosano-san!

09:43.510 --> 09:47.130
Special Ability: Thou Shalt Not Die.

09:44.890 --> 09:48.440
<b>Thou Shalt Not Die</b>

09:52.110 --> 09:54.290
Francis betrayed us?

09:54.290 --> 09:55.870
The transaction was a trap.

09:56.160 --> 10:00.070
I thought you two were both 
blown up with the car.

10:00.550 --> 10:01.950
That's impossible.

10:02.320 --> 10:05.530
Francis is arrogant, but he 
looks after his employees.

10:05.870 --> 10:07.820
Even if he was going to frame the Agency,

10:07.820 --> 10:10.370
he would only do it after 
Margaret-san's treatment.

10:10.750 --> 10:11.930
<i>Good point.</i>

10:12.660 --> 10:17.090
<i>So how did the military police find out 
where the transaction was taking place?</i>

10:17.090 --> 10:19.420
Let's get out of here first.

10:19.420 --> 10:20.560
Driver, please...

10:23.010 --> 10:24.130
Ambush!

10:24.130 --> 10:25.010
Everyone, get out!

10:27.060 --> 10:28.180
It's him.

10:36.270 --> 10:37.730
Go, Atsushi.

10:37.730 --> 10:39.470
I'll deal with him.

10:39.470 --> 10:40.450
But...

10:40.800 --> 10:43.990
The three of us together might 
stand a chance of winning.

10:43.990 --> 10:45.750
Winning isn't important.

10:45.750 --> 10:48.340
What's important is protecting Margaret.

10:48.340 --> 10:49.500
She's already been treated.

10:49.800 --> 10:53.710
Deliver her to Francis before the 
military police close the roads.

10:53.710 --> 10:57.800
That's our only hope for reviving 
the Armed Detective Agency.

10:58.510 --> 11:00.210
I'll drive.

11:00.690 --> 11:02.340
Don't worry.

11:02.880 --> 11:04.730
I'm not good at dying.

11:07.040 --> 11:09.020
Please be safe.

11:12.730 --> 11:13.990
Now, then...

11:14.410 --> 11:17.690
First off, may I get a look at your face?

11:28.190 --> 11:32.950
Your ability, the justness of it, 
has taught me...

11:31.830 --> 11:32.960
<b><i>You are too just</i></b>

11:32.960 --> 11:35.920
<b><i>You are too just</i></b>

11:48.540 --> 11:50.230
Stay back, you dumb shits!

11:50.230 --> 11:51.810
Freaking hell, it's tough.

11:51.810 --> 11:53.390
Why are you lot here?

11:53.390 --> 11:55.740
The boss's orders are absolute.

12:01.840 --> 12:03.370
Old man, look out!

12:05.850 --> 12:09.300
My life of evil is little 
more than a clown show.

12:09.300 --> 12:14.590
Thus I have no intention of making 
way for your pretense of justice.

12:14.670 --> 12:20.170
<b>Falling Camellia</b>

12:15.030 --> 12:18.710
Special ability: Falling Camellia.

12:29.460 --> 12:30.930
Wow...

12:30.930 --> 12:33.670
The escape boat is in the 
underground drain ahead.

12:41.420 --> 12:42.490
Go!

12:44.680 --> 12:46.960
I can't hold him off for long.

12:46.960 --> 12:47.610
But...

12:48.410 --> 12:50.210
Go!

12:51.760 --> 12:53.090
We're going!

12:53.090 --> 12:55.360
Don't let his efforts go to waste!

13:03.170 --> 13:08.370
May my soul forever be with the Port Mafia.

13:28.560 --> 13:30.980
<i>The character for "true"...</i>

13:42.310 --> 13:45.560
Only the Port Mafia can 
unlock this blast door.

13:46.090 --> 13:47.750
I'm not so sure.

13:47.750 --> 13:49.570
You...

13:49.570 --> 13:52.350
You seem to know about that Gifted.

13:52.970 --> 13:55.680
<i>The Hunting Dogs are military veterans.</i>

13:55.680 --> 13:58.760
<i>And that ability to manipulate metal...</i>

13:59.140 --> 14:01.400
Besides, she's an angel of death.

14:01.400 --> 14:04.020
The world's better off without her.

14:04.020 --> 14:06.090
<i>If that man is a Hunting Dog,</i>

14:06.090 --> 14:10.150
<i>it would make sense that they know 
about the name "angel of death."</i>

14:12.310 --> 14:13.240
<i>But...</i>

14:15.300 --> 14:17.870
<i>That man was most certainly dead.</i>

14:19.010 --> 14:22.850
<i>I tried so many times to bring him back. 
I know better than anyone.</i>

14:28.010 --> 14:29.300
That should do it.

14:29.860 --> 14:32.400
Even if the enemy uses a 
special ability to open the door,

14:32.400 --> 14:35.050
this proximity bomb will 
blow their heads off.

14:35.730 --> 14:38.040
Even a Hunting Dog would be dead instantly.

14:38.040 --> 14:40.720
I've checked the waterway bulkheads, as well.

14:42.650 --> 14:44.250
We're safe here.

14:47.680 --> 14:50.240
You two escape by boat.

14:50.240 --> 14:51.850
I'll stay here.

14:51.850 --> 14:53.040
What?!

14:53.040 --> 14:55.930
That man is only trying 
to get revenge on me.

14:55.930 --> 14:59.730
I can't let any more lives 
be lost because of me.

14:59.730 --> 15:02.010
Are you dissing us?

15:02.240 --> 15:06.000
We wouldn't be in the Port Mafia
 if we were such wimps.

15:07.930 --> 15:10.280
I have a badass older brother.

15:11.830 --> 15:14.450
I hated being compared to him.

15:14.450 --> 15:16.730
I turned to crime so that I could 
go in the opposite direction.

15:16.990 --> 15:22.120
But fighting and doing bad shit never 
relieved me of this indescribable agony.

15:23.510 --> 15:24.810
Then, one day...

15:26.330 --> 15:29.350
I was caught breaking into a safe
 owned by some serious crooks.

15:30.220 --> 15:35.110
They told me they'd spare my life, 
but I'd have to be a grunt for them.

15:36.210 --> 15:39.930
Work was fun, as strange as that is to say.

15:40.740 --> 15:43.410
When I was fighting as part 
of a powerful organization,

15:43.980 --> 15:48.490
I was neither my brother nor his 
opposite, but someone else entirely.

15:50.010 --> 15:52.330
The orders made me who I am.

15:52.970 --> 15:57.490
So, if my orders kill me today, 
I would have no regrets.

15:57.990 --> 15:59.170
Tachihara...

16:00.460 --> 16:01.970
What is it, Gin?

16:01.970 --> 16:04.220
Did my story move you?

16:06.700 --> 16:07.800
Hey!

16:12.350 --> 16:13.440
Run!

16:13.440 --> 16:14.980
I can't control the sword!

16:28.270 --> 16:29.340
Impossible...

16:29.610 --> 16:31.730
The door wasn't opened and 
the bomb never went off.

16:31.730 --> 16:32.910
How...?

16:41.260 --> 16:45.860
You finally became someone when 
you joined the organization...

16:46.980 --> 16:48.090
I get you.

16:49.410 --> 16:50.730
Come on!

16:50.730 --> 16:52.680
You wretched ghost of the past...

16:53.130 --> 16:57.240
I, Yosano Akiko, will wreck you!

16:58.320 --> 17:01.200
Do you know the fifth member 
of the Hunting Dogs?

17:01.200 --> 17:03.860
That came out of nowhere.

17:05.640 --> 17:08.030
The answer is no.

17:08.030 --> 17:11.340
I couldn't find anything about him, 
no matter how hard I tried.

17:11.940 --> 17:14.570
The fifth member of the Hunting Dogs...

17:15.020 --> 17:18.080
Master of metals and
 executioner of the shadows...

17:18.080 --> 17:22.570
A man who has an old, fateful connection 
with the Armed Detective Agency.

17:23.030 --> 17:27.800
How many of the Agency 
members will survive against him?

17:45.110 --> 17:46.870
<i>Did he stop the bullets?</i>

17:47.370 --> 17:51.370
<i>His ability to control metals is way 
more powerful than it used to be.</i>

17:51.370 --> 17:55.650
<i>Whether it's a gun or a sword, 
all weapons are his to control.</i>

17:55.650 --> 17:57.440
<i>I have no way of attacking him.</i>

18:20.010 --> 18:21.750
Today's a good day.

18:23.070 --> 18:28.050
The president and Rampo-san both 
forgave me despite knowing my sins.

18:28.640 --> 18:30.860
I was the one who couldn't forgive myself.

18:31.370 --> 18:34.790
But today, you came to take revenge on me.

18:35.290 --> 18:39.410
Thanks to you, I'm no longer lonely!

18:51.490 --> 18:52.930
That won't work!

18:58.230 --> 19:02.740
You can't stop an explosion 
with your ability, can you?

19:03.390 --> 19:07.980
I'll save the Agency and 
accept my punishment!

19:17.670 --> 19:18.700
What...

19:18.960 --> 19:20.820
It's not a bomb!

19:23.770 --> 19:26.040
A metal mannequin?

19:26.040 --> 19:28.360
Was the enemy never even here?

19:28.760 --> 19:29.600
<i>No...</i>

19:29.600 --> 19:32.970
<i>He couldn't have fought the 
way he did without seeing me.</i>

19:33.460 --> 19:36.940
<i>So the enemy's been watching 
from close by the whole time.</i>

19:37.580 --> 19:38.870
<i>Hold on...</i>

19:38.870 --> 19:41.420
<i>I remember this mannequin.</i>

19:44.530 --> 19:46.830
<i>It's the one I saw earlier.</i>

20:05.490 --> 20:07.180
Good work.

20:11.250 --> 20:12.940
Hunting Dogs!

20:14.120 --> 20:16.090
<i>Suddenly, I understand</i>

20:16.800 --> 20:19.810
<i>how they were able to follow me 
so accurately through the maze</i>

20:19.810 --> 20:21.990
<i>of this underground Port Mafia passage.</i>

20:22.890 --> 20:25.690
<i>And how the enemy passed through the door.</i>

20:26.740 --> 20:28.650
<i>And why the bomb was a fake.</i>

20:29.370 --> 20:32.220
<i>There's only one possible answer.</i>

20:38.800 --> 20:42.830
As a former medic who knew 
numerous military secrets,

20:42.830 --> 20:45.560
Mori Ougai was a dangerous man.

20:45.930 --> 20:49.950
I never would have expected that the 
undercover agent we sent to watch him

20:49.950 --> 20:52.270
would prove so useful.

20:53.150 --> 20:57.520
You had to work as a grunt for 
some serious crooks, you said?

20:57.520 --> 21:03.020
I thought you were talking 
about the Port Mafia.

21:03.640 --> 21:05.150
Nope.

21:06.690 --> 21:08.650
I'm the fifth Hunting Dog.

21:09.440 --> 21:12.700
Undercover agent Tachihara Michizou.

21:13.940 --> 21:19.580
And the soldier you killed fourteen 
years ago was my older brother.

21:21.720 --> 21:23.290
Your brother...

21:24.310 --> 21:25.840
If it weren't for you,

21:26.290 --> 21:29.970
I would never have had a chance to 
meet my parents and brother again.

21:30.680 --> 21:34.710
Because Sakaguchi, the previous agent, left,

21:34.710 --> 21:37.690
the military police decided to send 
another agent into the Port Mafia.

21:37.690 --> 21:40.070
But I asked for it specifically.

21:40.070 --> 21:43.700
I was sure I could get close 
to you if I was in the Mafia.

21:45.210 --> 21:47.150
Revenge for your brother.

21:49.470 --> 21:50.630
I see.

21:51.520 --> 21:53.770
Today is truly a good day.

21:55.120 --> 21:56.640
Do as you wish.

23:37.730 --> 23:39.970
Next Episode: 47

23:37.730 --> 23:39.970
<i>Jailbreak</i>
